      "note": "<p>PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, reconciled from two independent proposals. Binding HGM fields attest gnyis pa/second part and khas mi len/deny as lexical units: the former keeps the contained gnyis/second member, and the latter is a complete negative verb, with no invented negation null. mi dge/non-virtue retains mi/non and dge/virtue inside the hyphenated compound; non is bounded by a hyphen, not an added subword exception. The established autocommentary title and beginningless-time compound retain unique tighter members. 'khor bar/suffering cycle of life is the source's contextual rendering of cyclic life; the glossary for the inflected form contains in the circle of suffering life, not this exact English string. yongs su smin pa/ripened is directly HGM-attested.</p><p>Suppose advances beyond the bracketed editorial explanation: foundation consciousness and all four mental seeds select the translated argument, not bracketed repeats. de 'dra ba/same thing is a complete anaphoric similarity phrase at d3; neither the supplied quotations noun nor mention is assigned to a false atom. The later de in de yang does not own the dummy it in it would be incorrect to say: that it has no anaphoric referent. The continuative yang supplies And. The first final gzhi is banked once as basis, leaving its synonymous restatement or place unwrapped; the second owns place in What ... this place. Final yin zhe na, repeated seeds/planted, and distributed quotation/question framing are omitted rather than falsely nulled. Articles, you, passive auxiliaries and by people/themselves remain unwrapped. Exact C16 text and shorter or differently translated ILL parallels establish no correction or publication independence; no erratum is proposed.</p>"
